{{was wotd|2006|October|17}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}}, from Old French, from the {{etyl|roa-oit}} ''cavalcata'' from ''cavalcare'', which meant to ride on horseback, from Medieval Latin ''caballicāre'', from the Vulgar {{etyl|la}} ''[[caballus]]'', which means [[horse]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkævəlˌkeɪd/|/ˌkævəlˈkeɪd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-cavalcade.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[company]] of [[rider]]s.
# A [[parade]].
# A [[trail ride]], usually more than one day long.
# {{by extension}} A [[series]], a [[chain]] (e.g. of events).
#: ''As soon as I visited this website, a '''cavalcade''' of dialog boxes started to appear on my screen; that's when I realized my computer was infected with a virus. ''
====Synonyms====
* {{italbrac|company of riders}}: [[company]]
* {{italbrac|parade}}: [[parade]], [[procession]]

